pedia/pechenegs"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pechenegs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pechenegs</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pechenegs were a Turkic nomadic people who dominated the steppes north of the Black Sea from the late 9th century, after driving the Magyars westward.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pechina"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pechina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pechina</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pechina, called Bajjana in Arabic, is a town in the province of Almería in Andalusia, Spain, in the lower Andarax valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pechora-river"><span class="enc-name">Pechora River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pechora is a river of northern European Russia, about 1,800 kilometres long, rising in the northern Urals and flowing north into the Barents Sea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pecs"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pecs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pécs</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pécs is a city of southern Hungary, the centre of Baranya county, at the foot of the Mecsek hills.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pedakomati-vema-reddi"><span class="enc-name">Pedakomati Vema Reddi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pedakomati Vema Reddi was a king of the Reddi dynasty of coastal Andhra, ruling from Kondavidu from about 1403 to 1420.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pedanius-dioscorides"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedanius-dioscorides.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pedanius Dioscorides</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pedanius Dioscorides was a Greek physician from Anazarbus in Cilicia who served with the Roman army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pedda-soma-bhupal"><span class="enc-name">Pedda Soma Bhupal</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pedda Soma Bhupal was a local chief who founded the Gadwal samasthan around 1663 in the land between the Krishna and Tungabhadra rivers, in today's Telangana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pedieos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedieos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pedieos</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pedieos is the longest river of Cyprus, rising in the Troodos mountains and flowing north-east through Nicosia across the Mesaoria plain towards Famagusta Bay.</span></a></li></ul>
